1
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:34,824
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]:
<i>Who brings us this token of darkness?
<font color="#00bd00">(Man ammen toltha i dann hen morn?)</font></i>

2
00:00:31,334 --> 00:00:34,326
GALADRIEL [IN SINDARIN]:
<font color="#00bd00"><i>I amar prestar aen.</i></font>

3
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:36,401
[IN WESTRON] <i>The
world is changed.</i>

4
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:37,764
<font color="#00bd00"><i>Han mathon ne nen.</i></font>

5
00:00:37,342 --> 00:00:47,992
{\an8}<i>We will now fall. What should shall be.
<font color="#00bd00">(Si dannatha. Nauva.)</font></i>

6
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:39,859
<i>I feel it in the water.</i>

7
00:00:39,883 --> 00:00:41,518
<font color="#00bd00"><i>Han mathon ne chae.</i></font>

8
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,711
<i>I feel it in the earth.</i>

9
00:00:43,735 --> 00:00:46,021
<font color="#00bd00"><i>A han noston ned 'wilith.</i></font>

10
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:49,049
<i>I smell it in the air.</i>

11
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,343
<i>Much that once was...</i>

12
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,136
<i>...is lost.</i>

13
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,848
<i>For none now live who remember it.</i>

14
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:14,157
<i>It began with the forging
of the Great Rings.</i>

15
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:16,326
<i>Three were given to the Elves:</i>

16
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:20,289
<i>Immortal, wisest and fairest
of all beings.</i>

17
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,417
<i>Seven to the Dwarf-lords:</i>

18
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:28,589
<i>Great miners and craftsmen
of the mountain halls.</i>

19
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:30,299
<i>And nine...</i>

20
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>...nine rings were gifted
to the race of Men...</i>

21
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:37,556
<i>...who, above all else, desire power.</i>

22
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:43,895
<i>For within these rings was bound
the strength and will to govern each race.</i>

23
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:48,567
<i>But they were all of them deceived.</i>

24
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,902
<i>For another ring was made.</i>

25
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:55,324
<i>In the land of Mordor,
in the fires of Mount Doom...</i>

26
00:01:55,741 --> 00:02:00,203
<i>...the Dark Lord Sauron forged
in secret a Master Ring...</i>

27
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:02,456
<i>...to control all others.</i>

28
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:06,627
<i>And into this Ring he poured
his cruelty, his malice...</i>

29
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:11,048
<i>...and his will to dominate all life.</i>

30
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:15,886
<i>One Ring to rule them all.</i>

31
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,388
<i>One by one...</i>

32
00:02:18,597 --> 00:02:23,268
<i>...the Free Lands of Middle-earth
fell to the power of the Ring.</i>

33
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:26,521
<i>But there were some who resisted.</i>

34
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:31,652
<i>A Last Alliance of Men and Elves
marched against the armies of Mordor.</i>

35
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:36,490
<i>And on the slopes of Mount Doom, they
fought for the freedom of Middle-earth.</i>

36
00:02:43,086 --> 00:02:46,977
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

37
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:53,930
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

38
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:50,347
[IN SINDARIN] Hold positions!
<font color="#00bd00">(Tangado haid!)</font>

39
00:02:51,847 --> 00:02:53,647
Release the arrows!
<font color="#00bd00">(Leithio i philinn!)</font>

40
00:02:54,051 --> 00:02:57,825
{\an8}<i>The Lords of Unending Life
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâ Katharâd)</font></i>

41
00:02:54,149 --> 00:02:54,971
Positions!
<font color="#00bd00">(Haid!)</font>

42
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:04,820
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nidir nênâ)</font></i>

43
00:03:04,844 --> 00:03:11,988
{\an8}<i>We renounce the darkness
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbîtham [dâ]ur)</font></i>

44
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:09,439
<i>Victory was near.</i>

45
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:15,946
<i>But the power of the Ring...</i>

46
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,198
<i>...could not be undone.</i>

47
00:03:27,128 --> 00:03:31,058
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

48
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:38,945
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

49
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:44,725
<i>It was in this moment...</i>

50
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,310
<i>...when all hope had faded...</i>

51
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:51,648
<i>...that Isildur, son of the king,
took up his father's sword.</i>

52
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:29,227
<i>Sauron, the enemy of the Free Peoples
of Middle-earth, was defeated.</i>

53
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:38,278
<i>The Ring passed to Isildur...</i>

54
00:04:38,487 --> 00:04:42,699
<i>...who had this one chance
to destroy evil forever.</i>

55
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,535
<i>But the hearts of Men...</i>

56
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,246
<i>...are easily corrupted.</i>

57
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:53,126
<i>And the Ring of Power
has a will of its own.</i>

58
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,946
<i>It betrayed Isildur...</i>

59
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,200
<i>...to his death.</i>

60
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:33,250
<i>And some things
that should not have been forgotten...</i>

61
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,794
<i>...were lost.</i>

62
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:38,839
<i>History became legend...</i>

63
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,049
<i>...legend became myth.</i>

64
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:44,135
<i>And for
two and a half thousand years...</i>

65
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:48,014
<i>...the Ring passed
out of all knowledge.</i>

66
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,476
<i>Until, when chance came...</i>

67
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,272
<i>...it ensnared a new bearer.</i>

68
00:05:56,606 --> 00:06:01,444
GOLLUM:
My precious.

69
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:04,239
GALADRIEL: <i> The Ring came
to the creature Gollum...</i>

70
00:06:01,963 --> 00:06:15,882
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN QUENYA]: <i> The Herald of Death
<font color="#0078bd">(Tercáno Nuruva)</font></i>

71
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:08,326
<i>...who took it deep into the tunnels
of the Misty Mountains.</i>

72
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,496
<i>And there it consumed him.</i>

73
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,790
GOLLUM:
It came to me.

74
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:18,420
My own. My love. My own.

75
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:23,341
My precious.

76
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:30,390
GALADRIEL: <i> The Ring brought
to Gollum unnatural long life.</i>

77
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:34,436
<i>For 500 years it poisoned his mind.</i>

78
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:39,232
<i>And in the gloom of Gollum's cave,
it waited.</i>

79
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:42,694
<i>Darkness crept back
into the forests of the world.</i>

80
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:45,780
<i>Rumor grew of a shadow in the East...</i>

81
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:48,783
<i>...whispers of a nameless fear.</i>

82
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:52,287
<i>And the Ring of Power perceived...</i>

83
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:55,290
<i>...its time had now come.</i>

84
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,378
<i>It abandoned Gollum.</i>

85
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:05,550
<i>But something happened then
the Ring did not intend.</i>

86
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:10,972
<i>It was picked up by the most unlikely
creature imaginable.</i>

87
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,223
BILBO:
What's this?

88
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:13,892
GALADRIEL:
<i>A Hobbit.</i>

89
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:16,811
<i>Bilbo Baggins of the Shire.</i>

90
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,772
A ring.

91
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,857
GOLLUM:
Lost!

92
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,072
My precious is lost!

93
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,574
GALADRIEL:
<i>For the time will soon come...</i>

94
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:34,996
<i>...when Hobbits will shape
the fortunes of all.</i>

95
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:42,837
BILBO:
The 22nd day of September...

96
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,214
...in the year 1400...

97
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,051
...by Shire-reckoning.

98
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:54,140
Bag End, Bagshot Row, Hobbiton,
Westfarthing...

99
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:56,893
...the Shire...

100
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:59,896
...Middle-earth.

101
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:07,862
The Third Age of this world.

102
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:23,420
<i>There and Back Again:</i>

103
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,797
<i>A Hobbit's Tale.</i>

104
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:28,466
By Bilbo Baggins.

105
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:36,474
Now...

106
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,185
...where to begin?

107
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,521
Ah, yes...

108
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:47,694
"Concerning...

109
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,530
...Hobbits."

110
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:55,201
<i>Hobbits have been living and farming
in the four Farthings of the Shire...</i>

111
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,370
<i>...for many hundreds of years...</i>

112
00:08:57,537 --> 00:09:00,498
<i>...quite content to ignore
and be ignored...</i>

113
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:03,877
<i>...by the world of the Big Folk.</i>

114
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:09,883
<i>Middle-earth being, after all,
full of strange creatures beyond count...</i>

115
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:13,219
<i>...Hobbits must seem
of little importance...</i>

116
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:17,432
<i>...being neither renowned
as great warriors...</i>

117
00:09:17,599 --> 00:09:21,811
<i>...nor counted among the very wise.</i>

118
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:25,774
[KNOCKING]

119
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,194
Frodo! Someone at the door.

120
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,947
<i>In fact, it has been remarked by some...</i>

121
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:37,660
<i>...that Hobbits' only real passion
is for food.</i>

122
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,205
<i>A rather unfair observation...</i>

123
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:44,084
<i>...as we have also developed a keen
interest in the brewing of ales...</i>

124
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:47,212
<i>...and the smoking of pipe-weed.</i>

125
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:50,507
<i>But where our hearts truly lie...</i>

126
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:52,842
<i>...is in peace and quiet...</i>

127
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:55,678
<i>...and good, tilled earth.</i>

128
00:09:55,845 --> 00:10:01,059
<i>For all Hobbits share a love
of things that grow.</i>

129
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:08,608
<i>And, yes, no doubt to others,
our ways seem quaint.</i>

130
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:14,030
<i>But today of all days,
it is brought home to me:</i>

131
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:20,495
<i>It is no bad thing
to celebrate a simple life.</i>

132
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,623
[KNOCKING]

133
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:27,877
Frodo, the door!

134
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:32,924
Sticklebacks. Where is that boy?

135
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,552
Frodo!

136
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:44,894
MALE VOICE:
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

137
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:48,940
[WAGON RUMBLES]

138
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:53,403
<i>And I must follow if I can</i>

139
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:58,491
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

140
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:02,245
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

141
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:07,375
<i>Now far ahead the road has gone</i>

142
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:11,796
<i>-And I must follow if I can</i>
-You're late.

143
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,887
A wizard is never late, Frodo Baggins.

144
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:24,309
Nor is he early. He arrives
precisely when he means to.

145
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,781
It's wonderful to see you, Gandalf!

146
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:46,331
You didn't think I'd miss
your Uncle Bilbo's birthday?

147
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:50,168
How is the old rascal?

148
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:54,214
I hear it's going to be a party
of special magnificence.

149
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:56,841
You know Bilbo.
He's got the whole place in an uproar.

150
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:59,010
Well, that should please him.

151
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:01,012
Half the Shire's been invited.

152
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:03,932
And the rest of them are turning up
anyway.

153
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:10,396
BILBO:
<i>And so life in the Shire goes on...</i>

154
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:13,650
<i>...very much as it has
this past Age...</i>

155
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:19,364
<i>...full of its own comings and goings,
with change coming slowly.</i>

156
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,449
<i>If it comes at all.</i>

157
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:26,162
<i>For things are made to endure
in the Shire...</i>

158
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:29,832
<i>...passing from one generation
to the next.</i>

159
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:35,213
<i>There's always been a Baggins
living here under the Hill...</i>

160
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,714
<i>...in Bag End.</i>

161
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:42,345
And there always will be.

162
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:46,391
To tell you the truth,
Bilbo's been a bit odd lately.

163
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,019
I mean, more than usual.

164
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,981
He's taken to locking himself
in his study.

165
00:12:54,524 --> 00:12:58,695
<i>He spends hours poring over old maps
when he thinks I'm not looking.</i>

166
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:13,042
Where's it gone?

167
00:13:39,569 --> 00:13:41,904
He's up to something.

168
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,540
-All right, then. Keep your secrets.
-What?

169
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:54,417
But I know you have something
to do with it.

170
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:55,752
Good gracious me.

171
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,254
Before you came along, we Bagginses
were very well thought of.

172
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,089
Indeed.

173
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,592
Never had any adventures
or did anything unexpected.

174
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:09,098
If you're referring to the incident
with the dragon, I was barely involved.

175
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:12,852
All I did was give your uncle
a little nudge out of the door.

176
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:17,106
Whatever you did, you've been officially
labeled a disturber of the peace.

177
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,442
Oh, really?

178
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,033
Gandalf! Gandalf!

179
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:30,620
[CHILDREN SHOUTING]

180
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,374
FEMALE HOBBIT 1:
Fireworks, Gandalf!

181
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,046
FEMALE HOBBIT 2: Gandalf!
MALE HOBBIT: Fireworks, Gandalf!

182
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,941
Gandalf?

183
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:04,612
-I'm glad you're back.
-So am I, dear boy.

184
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,827
So am I.

185
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,472
Whoa, whoa.

186
00:15:42,692 --> 00:15:44,193
BILBO:
No, thank you!

187
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:48,322
We don't want any more visitors,
well-wishers or distant relations!

188
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:52,034
And what about very old friends?

189
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,873
Gandalf?

190
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:01,043
-Bilbo Baggins.
-My dear Gandalf!

191
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:06,382
Good to see you. 111 years old!
Who would believe it?

192
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,136
You haven't aged a day.

193
00:16:16,726 --> 00:16:18,728
Come on, come in!

194
00:16:18,895 --> 00:16:21,355
Welcome, welcome.

195
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:25,067
Oh, here we are.

196
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:29,197
Tea? Or maybe something
a little stronger?

197
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:33,159
I've got a few bottles
of the Old Winyard left. 1296.

198
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:37,413
Very good year. Almost as old as I am.

199
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:43,085
It was laid down by my father.
What say we open one, eh?

200
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:45,922
Just tea, thank you.

201
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,094
Oh!

202
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,930
I was expecting you sometime
last week.

203
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:57,433
Not that it matters. You come and go as
you please. Always have and always will.

204
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:02,939
You caught me a bit unprepared. We've
only got cold chicken and a bit of pickle...

205
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:06,442
There's some cheese here.
No, that won't do.

206
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:10,613
We've got raspberry jam,
an apple tart...

207
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:15,243
But not much for afters.
Oh, no, we're all right.

208
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:18,287
I've just found some sponge cake.

209
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:22,542
I could make you some eggs
if you'd--

210
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,965
-Just tea, thank you.
-Oh, right.

211
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,468
-You don't mind if I eat, do you?
-No, not at all.

212
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:33,970
[KNOCKING]

213
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,429
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!

214
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,223
I'm not at home!

215
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,815
It's the Sackville-Bagginses.

216
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:48,109
-I know you're in there!
-They're after the house.

217
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:51,279
They've never forgiven me
for living this long.

218
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,282
I've got to get away from these confounded
relatives, hanging on the bell all day...

219
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,325
...never giving me a moment's peace.

220
00:17:57,118 --> 00:18:00,663
I want to see mountains again.
Mountains, Gandalf!

221
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:05,334
And then find somewhere quiet
where I can finish my book. Oh, tea.

222
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:09,505
-So you mean to go through with your plan?
-Yes, yes. It's all in hand.

223
00:18:09,672 --> 00:18:11,966
All the arrangements are made.

224
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,511
Oh, thank you.

225
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,347
Frodo suspects something.

226
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:21,017
Of course he does. He's a Baggins...

227
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,853
...not some block headed Bracegirdle
from Hardbottle.

228
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,189
You will tell him, won't you?

229
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:30,151
-Yes, yes.
-He's very fond of you.

230
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:33,863
I know.

231
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,535
He'd probably come with me
if I asked him.

232
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,664
I think in his heart, Frodo's
still in love with the Shire.

233
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:47,543
The woods, the fields.

234
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:50,046
Little rivers.

235
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:57,219
I am old, Gandalf.

236
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:03,893
I know I don't look it, but I'm
beginning to feel it in my heart.

237
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,564
I feel thin.

238
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:10,399
Sort of stretched...

239
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:15,071
...like butter scraped
over too much bread.

240
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:19,742
I need a holiday. A very long holiday.

241
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:23,204
And I don't expect I shall return.

242
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:28,584
In fact, I mean not to.

243
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:35,383
Old Toby. The finest weed
in the Southfarthing.

244
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:51,732
Ah.

245
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,277
Gandalf, my old friend...

246
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:58,280
...this will be a night to remember.

247
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,826
[CHEERING]

248
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:06,122
[MUSIC PLAYS]

249
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,138
BILBO:
Hello, hello.

250
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:26,475
Fatty Bolger. Lovely to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

251
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:30,104
Go on, Sam. Ask Rosie for a dance.

252
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:36,277
-I think I'll just have another ale.
-Oh, no, you don't.

253
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:39,113
Go on!

254
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:51,000
So there I was...

255
00:20:51,292 --> 00:20:55,337
...at the mercy
of three monstrous trolls.

256
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,506
And they were all arguing
amongst themselves...

257
00:20:57,673 --> 00:21:00,134
...about how they were
going to cook us.

258
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:05,347
Whether it be turned on a spit, or to sit
on us one by one, squash us into jelly.

259
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:09,935
They spent so much time arguing
the whithertos and the whyfors...

260
00:21:10,144 --> 00:21:13,689
...that the sun's first light
crept over the top of the trees...

261
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,193
...and turned them all to stone!

262
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,362
[LAUGHS]

263
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:23,866
MERRY:
Quickly.

264
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:27,828
Whoa!

265
00:21:28,037 --> 00:21:30,039
Up they go!

266
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,210
No, the big one.

267
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:46,222
Mrs. Bracegirdle, how nice to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

268
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:48,349
Are all these children yours?

269
00:21:48,516 --> 00:21:51,519
Good gracious,
you have been productive.

270
00:21:53,521 --> 00:21:54,855
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo?

271
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,234
Sackville-Bagginses!

272
00:21:58,484 --> 00:21:59,568
Quickly, hide!

273
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:11,580
Thank you, my boy.

274
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:15,501
You're a good lad, Frodo.

275
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,588
I'm very selfish, you know.

276
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:23,425
Yes, I am. Very selfish.

277
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:25,845
I don't know why I took you in
after your mother and father died...

278
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:27,555
...but it wasn't out of charity.

279
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:29,723
I think it was because...

280
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:32,226
...of all my numerous relations...

281
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:36,021
...you were the one Baggins
that showed real spirit.

282
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:38,107
Bilbo, have you been
at the Gaffer's home brew?

283
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:40,025
No.

284
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,945
Well, yes, but that's not the point.

285
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:46,407
The point is, Frodo...

286
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,453
...you'll be all right.

287
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,959
-Done!
-You're supposed to stick it in the ground.

288
00:22:57,126 --> 00:22:58,627
-It is in the ground.
-Outside!

289
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,296
This was your idea.

290
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:17,646
Bilbo.

291
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:21,650
Bilbo, watch out for the dragon!

292
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:25,154
Nonsense. There hasn't been a dragon
in these parts for a thousand years.

293
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:42,338
-That was good.
-Let's get another one.

294
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:48,093
GANDALF:
Meriadoc Brandybuck and Peregrin Took.

295
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,137
I might've known.

296
00:23:56,018 --> 00:23:58,103
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Speech, Bilbo!

297
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,314
MALE HOBBIT:
Speech!

298
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,607
Speech!

299
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:09,156
My dear Bagginses and Boffins...

300
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:12,159
...Tooks and Brandybucks...

301
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:14,828
...Grubbs, Chubbs...

302
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:16,080
...Hornblowers...

303
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,874
...Bolgers...

304
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,834
...Bracegirdles...

305
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:23,671
-...and Proudfoots.
-Proudfeet!

306
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:29,009
Today is my 111th birthday!

307
00:24:30,803 --> 00:24:32,346
Happy birthday!

308
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:36,850
But alas, eleventy-one years is
far too short a time to live among...

309
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:39,895
...such excellent
and admirable Hobbits.

310
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:43,565
I don't know half of you
half as well as I should like...

311
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:48,362
...and I like less than half of you
half as well as you deserve.

312
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,492
I, uh--

313
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,708
I have things to do.

314
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:09,216
I've put this off far too long.

315
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:17,016
I regret to announce this is the end!

316
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,351
I'm going now.

317
00:25:20,436 --> 00:25:23,355
I bid you all a very fond farewell.

318
00:25:25,733 --> 00:25:26,942
Goodbye.

319
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,450
[HOBBITS CLAMORING]

320
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:39,288
[FOOTSTEPS]

321
00:25:50,132 --> 00:25:52,217
[LAUGHS]

322
00:26:00,184 --> 00:26:03,312
I suppose you think
that was terribly clever.

323
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:06,899
Come on, Gandalf.
Did you see their faces?

324
00:26:07,066 --> 00:26:12,112
There are many magic rings in this world,
and none of them should be used lightly.

325
00:26:12,321 --> 00:26:14,490
It was just a bit of fun.

326
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:18,410
Oh, you're probably right, as usual.

327
00:26:19,787 --> 00:26:23,332
-You will keep an eye on Frodo, won't you?
-Two eyes.

328
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:26,210
As often as I can spare them.

329
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:29,588
-I'm leaving everything to him.
-What about this ring of yours?

330
00:26:29,797 --> 00:26:33,133
-Is that staying too?
-Yes, yes.

331
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:37,638
It's in an envelope over there
on the mantelpiece.

332
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:41,683
No. Wait, it's...

333
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,855
...here in my pocket.

334
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:54,738
Isn't that--? Isn't that odd, now?

335
00:26:56,365 --> 00:26:59,868
Yet, after all, why not?

336
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:06,333
-Why shouldn't I keep it?
-I think you should leave the ring behind.

337
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,961
Is that so hard?

338
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:10,462
Well, no.

339
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,383
And yes.

340
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:19,388
Now it comes to it,
I don't feel like parting with it.

341
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,390
It's mine. I found it! It came to me!

342
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:25,811
-There's no need to get angry.
-Well, if I'm angry, it's your fault!

343
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:28,063
It's mine.

344
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,817
My own.

345
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:36,155
-My precious.
-Precious?

346
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:39,199
It's been called that before,
but not by you.

347
00:27:39,408 --> 00:27:41,994
What business is it of yours
what I do with my own things?

348
00:27:42,202 --> 00:27:44,913
I think you've had that ring
quite long enough.

349
00:27:45,164 --> 00:27:48,000
-You want it for yourself!
-Bilbo Baggins!

350
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:52,421
Do not take me for some conjurer
of cheap tricks.

351
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:56,341
I am not trying to rob you.

352
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,098
I'm trying to help you.

353
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:05,976
[BILBO WHIMPERS]

354
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:14,902
All your long years,
we've been friends.

355
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:17,446
Trust me as you once did.

356
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:21,116
Let it go.

357
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:24,661
You're right, Gandalf.

358
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:29,458
The ring must go to Frodo.

359
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:33,795
It's late. The road is long.

360
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:36,465
Yes, it is time.

361
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:41,303
-Bilbo.
-Hm?

362
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:44,306
The ring is still in your pocket.

363
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,602
Ah. Yes.

364
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:22,010
I've thought up an ending for my book:

365
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:28,684
"And he lived happily ever after
to the end of his days."

366
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:32,312
And I'm sure you will, my dear friend.

367
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:34,815
Goodbye, Gandalf.

368
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:40,195
Goodbye, dear Bilbo.

369
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:52,207
BILBO:
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

370
00:29:52,897 --> 00:29:56,126
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

371
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:57,129
Until our next meeting.
<i> </i>

372
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:28,201
BILBO:
<i>It's mine. My own.</i>

373
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:31,788
<i>My precious.</i>

374
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:35,000
Riddles in the dark.

375
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:36,626
Bilbo!

376
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:38,378
Bilbo!

377
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,926
My precious.

378
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:48,764
Precious.

379
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:51,516
He's gone, hasn't he?

380
00:30:54,269 --> 00:30:57,314
He talked for so long about leaving...

381
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:00,275
...I didn't think he'd really do it.

382
00:31:04,738 --> 00:31:06,615
Gandalf?

383
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:16,583
Bilbo's ring.

384
00:31:16,917 --> 00:31:19,294
He's gone to stay with the Elves.

385
00:31:19,461 --> 00:31:22,589
He's left you Bag End.

386
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:28,762
Along with all his possessions.

387
00:31:28,929 --> 00:31:31,807
The ring is yours now.

388
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,938
-Put it somewhere out of sight.
-Where are you going?

389
00:31:38,105 --> 00:31:40,357
-There are some things that I must see to.
-What things?

390
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:44,820
-Questions. Questions that need answering.
-You've only just arrived.

391
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:48,323
I don't understand.

392
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:52,661
Neither do I.

393
00:31:55,956 --> 00:31:58,291
Keep it secret.

394
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:00,210
Keep it safe.

395
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,036
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

396
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:37,372
GOLLUM:
<i>Shire!</i>

397
00:32:37,706 --> 00:32:40,834
<i>Baggins!</i>

398
00:32:40,858 --> 00:32:49,708
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> We renounce our Maker.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâbîtham Magânanê)</font></i>

399
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:55,640
[THUNDER RUMBLES]

400
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:32,260
GANDALF:
<i>"The year 3434 of the Second Age.</i>

401
00:33:32,469 --> 00:33:36,890
<i>Here follows the account of Isildur,
High King of Gondor...</i>

402
00:33:37,090 --> 00:33:40,761
<i>...and the finding
of the Ring of Power."</i>

403
00:33:39,285 --> 00:33:54,435
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN QUENYA]: <i> The strength, the weapon
<font color="#0078bd">(I tuo I macil)</font></i>

404
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:46,107
<i>"It has come to me.</i>

405
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:49,778
<i>The One Ring. It shall be
an heirloom of my kingdom.</i>

406
00:33:49,945 --> 00:33:53,406
<i>All those who follow in my bloodline
shall be bound to its fate...</i>

407
00:33:53,615 --> 00:33:57,410
<i>...for I will risk
no hurt to the Ring.</i>

408
00:33:54,454 --> 00:34:10,964
{\an8}<i>Go to victory!
<font color="#0078bd">(Á lelyat túrenna!)</font></i>

409
00:33:57,619 --> 00:34:00,121
<i>It is precious to me...</i>

410
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:03,625
<i>...though I buy it with great pain.</i>

411
00:34:05,099 --> 00:34:08,128
VOICE OF THE RING [WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

412
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:10,966
<i>The markings upon the band
begin to fade.</i>

413
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:15,971
<i>The writing, which at first was as clear
as red flame, has all but disappeared.</i>

414
00:34:16,221 --> 00:34:20,267
<i>A secret now
that only fire can tell."</i>

415
00:34:24,813 --> 00:34:26,648
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

416
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:39,786
Shire.

417
00:34:39,953 --> 00:34:41,955
Baggins.

418
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:46,501
There's no Bagginses around here.
They're all up in Hobbiton.

419
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,671
That way.

420
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:57,887
<i>To heal my heart and drown my woe</i>

421
00:34:58,054 --> 00:35:00,390
<i>Rain may fall and wind may blow</i>

422
00:35:00,557 --> 00:35:02,517
<i>But there still be</i>

423
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:04,144
<i>Many miles to go</i>

424
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:06,271
<i>Sweet is the sound of the pouring rain</i>

425
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,648
<i>And the stream that falls
From hill to plain</i>

426
00:35:08,857 --> 00:35:10,692
<i>Better than rain or rippling brook</i>

427
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:13,278
<i>Is a mug of beer inside this Took</i>

428
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:19,534
There's been some strange folk
crossing the Shire.

429
00:35:19,993 --> 00:35:23,830
Dwarves and others of a less
than savory nature.

430
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:25,707
War is brewing.

431
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:29,210
The mountains are fair teeming
with goblins.

432
00:35:29,419 --> 00:35:32,047
Far-off tales and children's stories,
that's all that is.

433
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:36,718
You're beginning to sound like that old
Bilbo Baggins. Cracked, he was.

434
00:35:36,885 --> 00:35:39,888
Young Mr. Frodo here,
he's cracking.

435
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:41,514
And proud of it.

436
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,933
-Cheers, Gaffer.
-Cheers.

437
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:48,229
It's none of our concern what goes on
beyond our borders.

438
00:35:48,396 --> 00:35:52,734
Keep your nose out of trouble,
and no trouble'll come to you.

439
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:58,281
-Good night, lads.
-Good night.

440
00:35:58,448 --> 00:36:02,952
Good night, sweet maiden
of the golden ale.

441
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:05,538
Mind who you're sweet-talking.

442
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:10,251
Don't worry, Sam. Rosie knows an idiot
when she sees one.

443
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:12,420
Does she?

444
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:16,091
-Good night, Sam.
-Good night, Mr. Frodo.

445
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,368
Is it secret? Is it safe?

446
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:47,872
[PIG SQUEALS]

447
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:50,583
Ah.

448
00:36:52,252 --> 00:36:54,379
What are you doing?

449
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:09,477
Hold out your hand, Frodo.

450
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:10,812
It's quite cool.

451
00:37:14,399 --> 00:37:16,151
What can you see?

452
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,321
Can you see anything?

453
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,492
Nothing.

454
00:37:25,118 --> 00:37:27,120
There's nothing.

455
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,664
Wait.

456
00:37:31,554 --> 00:37:34,334
THE RING [WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

457
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:36,004
There are markings.

458
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:40,925
It's some form of Elvish.
I can't read it.

459
00:37:41,134 --> 00:37:43,678
There are few who can.

460
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:49,058
The language is that of Mordor,
which I will not utter here.

461
00:37:49,684 --> 00:37:50,727
Mordor!

462
00:37:51,019 --> 00:37:53,021
In the common tongue, it says:

463
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:56,733
"One Ring to rule them all...

464
00:37:57,025 --> 00:37:59,319
...One Ring to find them...

465
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:01,696
...One Ring to bring them all...

466
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:05,033
...and in the darkness bind them."

467
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,703
This is the One Ring...

468
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:14,167
...forged by the Dark Lord Sauron
in the fires of Mount Doom.

469
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:18,379
Taken by Isildur
from the hand of Sauron himself.

470
00:38:19,172 --> 00:38:21,716
Bilbo found it.

471
00:38:22,175 --> 00:38:24,093
-In Gollum's cave.
-Yes.

472
00:38:24,344 --> 00:38:28,890
For 60 years, the Ring lay quiet
in Bilbo's keeping...

473
00:38:29,057 --> 00:38:32,477
...prolonging his life,
delaying old age.

474
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:37,565
But no longer, Frodo.
Evil is stirring in Mordor.

475
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:40,109
The Ring has awoken.

476
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:43,071
It's heard its master's call.

477
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:47,200
But he was destroyed.
Sauron was destroyed.

478
00:38:47,929 --> 00:38:50,578
THE RING: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

479
00:38:52,914 --> 00:38:54,999
GANDALF:
No, Frodo.

480
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:59,254
The spirit of Sauron endured.

481
00:38:59,420 --> 00:39:04,759
His life force is bound to the Ring,
and the Ring survived.

482
00:39:05,093 --> 00:39:07,262
Sauron has returned.

483
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,265
His Orcs have multiplied.

484
00:39:10,431 --> 00:39:14,477
His fortress at Barad-dûr
is rebuilt in the land of Mordor.

485
00:39:14,644 --> 00:39:19,440
Sauron needs only this Ring to cover
all the lands in a second darkness.

486
00:39:19,649 --> 00:39:21,734
He is seeking it.

487
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:25,780
Seeking it. All his thought
is bent on it.

488
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:28,741
For the Ring yearns above all else...

489
00:39:28,950 --> 00:39:32,328
...to return to the hand
of its master.

490
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:34,330
They are one...

491
00:39:34,539 --> 00:39:37,625
...the Ring and the Dark Lord.

492
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:38,835
Frodo...

493
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:41,296
...he must never find it.

494
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,547
FRODO:
All right.

495
00:39:42,839 --> 00:39:47,176
We put it away. We keep it hidden.
We never speak of it again.

496
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:50,054
No one knows it's here, do they?

497
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:56,936
Do they, Gandalf?

498
00:39:57,979 --> 00:40:01,357
There is one other who knew
that Bilbo had the Ring.

499
00:40:02,650 --> 00:40:05,653
I looked everywhere
for the creature Gollum.

500
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:07,989
But the enemy found him first.

501
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:09,532
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

502
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:12,201
GANDALF: <i> I don't know how long
they tortured him.</i>

503
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:16,873
<i>But amidst the endless screams and
inane babble, they discerned two words:</i>

504
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:19,208
GOLLUM:
Shire!

505
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,002
Baggins!

506
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,046
Shire.

507
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:26,174
Baggins. But that would
lead them here!

508
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:30,011
Who goes there?

509
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:32,972
Take it, Gandalf!

510
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:34,390
-Take it!
-No, Frodo.

511
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:36,976
-You must take it!
-You cannot offer me this ring!

512
00:40:37,185 --> 00:40:40,521
-I'm giving it to you!
-Don't tempt me, Frodo!

513
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:44,233
I dare not take it.

514
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:47,028
Not even to keep it safe.

515
00:40:48,196 --> 00:40:50,198
Understand, Frodo...

516
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:54,494
...I would use this Ring
from a desire to do good.

517
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:05,630
But through me, it would wield a power
too great and terrible to imagine.

518
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:09,133
-But it cannot stay in the Shire!
-No.

519
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,637
No, it can't.

520
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,352
What must I do?

521
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:24,565
-You must leave. And leave quickly.
-Where? Where do I go?

522
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:28,027
Get out of the Shire.
Make for the village of Bree.

523
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,404
Bree.

524
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:32,365
-What about you?
-I'll be waiting for you...

525
00:41:32,573 --> 00:41:35,034
...at the inn of the Prancing Pony.

526
00:41:35,243 --> 00:41:38,955
-And the Ring will be safe there?
- I don't know, Frodo.

527
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,165
I don't have any answers.

528
00:41:42,667 --> 00:41:48,256
I must see the head of my order. He is
both wise and powerful. Trust me, Frodo.

529
00:41:48,423 --> 00:41:50,550
He'll know what to do.

530
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:53,970
You'll have to leave the name
of Baggins behind you.

531
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:56,764
That name is not safe
outside the Shire.

532
00:41:57,390 --> 00:42:00,685
Travel only by day.
And stay off the road.

533
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,480
I can cut across country
easily enough.

534
00:42:06,983 --> 00:42:08,317
My dear Frodo.

535
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:11,654
Hobbits really are amazing creatures.

536
00:42:11,821 --> 00:42:14,782
You can learn all that there is to
know about their ways in a month.

537
00:42:14,949 --> 00:42:17,326
And yet, after a hundred years...

538
00:42:17,493 --> 00:42:19,579
...they can still surprise you.

539
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:20,955
[RUSTLING]

540
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:22,498
Get down.

541
00:42:31,132 --> 00:42:32,258
[GROANING]

542
00:42:34,802 --> 00:42:38,264
Confound it all, Samwise Gamgee!
Have you been eavesdropping?

543
00:42:38,431 --> 00:42:42,935
I haven't been dropping no eaves. Honest.
I was cutting the grass under the window.

544
00:42:43,102 --> 00:42:45,521
A little late for trimming the verge,
don't you think?

545
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:48,608
-I heard raised voices.
-What did you hear? Speak!

546
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:49,859
Nothing important.

547
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:54,530
That is, I heard a good deal about a ring,
a Dark Lord and the end of the world but--

548
00:42:54,739 --> 00:42:59,494
Please, Mr. Gandalf, sir, don't hurt me.
Don't turn me into anything unnatural.

549
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:01,829
No?

550
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:04,165
Perhaps not.

551
00:43:05,374 --> 00:43:08,836
I've thought of a better use for you.

552
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:13,549
GANDALF:
Come along, Samwise. Keep up.

553
00:43:15,051 --> 00:43:17,345
Be careful, both of you.

554
00:43:17,553 --> 00:43:20,348
The enemy has many spies
in his service:

555
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:23,518
Birds, beasts.

556
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,063
Is it safe?

557
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,149
Never put it on...

558
00:43:30,358 --> 00:43:33,736
...for the agents of the Dark Lord
will be drawn to its power.

559
00:43:33,903 --> 00:43:35,404
Always remember, Frodo...

560
00:43:35,905 --> 00:43:39,075
...the Ring is trying to get back
to its master.

561
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:41,577
It wants to be found.

562
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:51,796
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

563
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:24,412
This is it.

564
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,914
This is what?

565
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:29,250
If I take one more step...

566
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:33,629
...it'll be the farthest away
from home I've ever been.

567
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:39,427
Come on, Sam.

568
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:49,645
Remember what Bilbo used to say:

569
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,983
-"It's a dangerous business, Frodo."
BILBO: <i>"Going out your door.</i>

570
00:44:54,150 --> 00:44:58,613
<i>You step onto the road,
and if you don't keep your feet...</i>

571
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:02,950
<i>...there's no knowing where
you might be swept off to."</i>

572
00:45:09,002 --> 00:45:16,807
{\an8}[WOOD-ELVES SING IN SINDARIN]:
<i>O Queen beyond the Western Seas!
<font color="#00bd00">(Rîn athar annún-aearath!)</font></i>

573
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:17,907
Sam.

574
00:45:18,251 --> 00:45:26,708
{\an8}<i>O light to us that wander
<font color="#00bd00">(Calad ammen i reniar)</font></i>

575
00:45:22,303 --> 00:45:23,429
Wood-elves.

576
00:45:28,008 --> 00:45:36,457
{\an8}<i>Amid the tree-woven lands of Middle-earth.
<font color="#00bd00">(Mi 'aladhremmin ennorath.)</font></i>

577
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:39,525
They're going to the harbor
beyond the White Towers.

578
00:45:38,119 --> 00:45:47,009
{\an8}<i>O Elbereth Star-kindler!
<font color="#00bd00">(A Elbereth Gilthoniel!)</font></i>

579
00:45:41,197 --> 00:45:42,664
To the Grey Havens.

580
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,618
SAM:
They're leaving Middle-earth.

581
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:47,333
FRODO:
Never to return.

582
00:45:47,763 --> 00:45:56,648
{\an8}<i>Your eyes and breath like shining jewels
<font color="#00bd00">(I chîn a thûl lín míriel)</font></i>

583
00:45:50,873 --> 00:45:52,089
I don't know why...

584
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:56,087
...it makes me sad.

585
00:45:58,172 --> 00:46:02,802
Everywhere I lie there's a dirty
great root sticking into my back.

586
00:46:03,511 --> 00:46:05,221
Just shut your eyes...

587
00:46:05,388 --> 00:46:08,182
...and imagine you're back
in your own bed...

588
00:46:08,349 --> 00:46:12,311
...with a soft mattress
and a lovely feather pillow.

589
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:24,323
It's not working, Mr. Frodo.

590
00:46:24,490 --> 00:46:27,368
I'm never going to be able
to sleep out here.

591
00:46:29,704 --> 00:46:32,039
Me neither, Sam.

592
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:03,612
MALE VOICE: <i> Smoke rises
from the Mountain of Doom.</i>

593
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:05,448
<i>The hour grows late.</i>

594
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:09,243
<i>And Gandalf the Grey
rides to Isengard...</i>

595
00:47:09,410 --> 00:47:11,871
<i>...seeking my counsel.</i>

596
00:47:12,079 --> 00:47:16,083
For that is why you have come,
is it not?

597
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:17,543
My old friend.

598
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:19,420
Saruman.

599
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:27,261
SARUMAN: You are sure of this?
GANDALF: Beyond any doubt.

600
00:47:28,054 --> 00:47:30,306
So the Ring of Power has been found.

601
00:47:30,473 --> 00:47:33,726
All these long years,
it was in the Shire.

602
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:37,063
-Under my very nose.
-Yet you did not have the wit to see it.

603
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:42,193
Your love of the halfling's leaf
has clearly slowed your mind.

604
00:47:43,069 --> 00:47:47,073
But we still have time. Time enough
to counter Sauron if we act quickly.

605
00:47:47,239 --> 00:47:48,699
Time?

606
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:52,244
What time do you think we have?

607
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:56,582
Sauron has regained
much of his former strength.

608
00:47:56,749 --> 00:47:58,959
He cannot yet take physical form...

609
00:47:59,210 --> 00:48:01,921
...but his spirit has lost
none of its potency.

610
00:48:02,588 --> 00:48:07,635
Concealed within his fortress,
the Lord of Mordor sees all.

611
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:14,141
His gaze pierces cloud, shadow,
earth and flesh.

612
00:48:15,643 --> 00:48:18,813
You know of what I speak, Gandalf.

613
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:24,985
A Great Eye, lidless,
wreathed in flame.

614
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:27,738
The Eye of Sauron.

615
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:30,533
He is gathering all evil to him.

616
00:48:30,741 --> 00:48:33,244
Very soon, he'll have summoned
an army great enough...

617
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:35,621
...for an assault upon Middle-earth.

618
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:38,332
You know this?

619
00:48:38,833 --> 00:48:40,334
How?

620
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,628
I have seen it.

621
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:46,257
A palantír is a dangerous tool,
Saruman.

622
00:48:46,966 --> 00:48:48,467
Why?

623
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:51,637
Why should we fear to use it?

624
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:58,185
They are not all accounted for,
the lost Seeing-stones.

625
00:48:58,352 --> 00:49:01,605
We do not know who else
may be watching.

626
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:06,944
The hour is later than you think.

627
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:09,447
Sauron's forces are already moving.

628
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:14,452
The Nine have left Minas Morgul.

629
00:49:14,827 --> 00:49:15,870
The Nine?

630
00:49:16,036 --> 00:49:19,123
They crossed the River Isen
on Midsummer's Eve...

631
00:49:19,290 --> 00:49:21,959
...disguised as riders in black.

632
00:49:22,168 --> 00:49:26,130
-They've reached the Shire?
-They will find the Ring.

633
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:29,967
And kill the one who carries it.

634
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:31,969
Frodo!

635
00:49:44,565 --> 00:49:48,986
You did not seriously think that a Hobbit
could contend with the will of Sauron?

636
00:49:49,737 --> 00:49:52,531
There are none who can.

637
00:49:55,034 --> 00:49:57,745
Against the power of Mordor...

638
00:49:57,912 --> 00:50:00,581
...there can be no victory.

639
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:05,711
We must join with him, Gandalf.

640
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:09,340
We must join with Sauron.

641
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:14,678
It would be wise, my friend.

642
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:16,597
Tell me...

643
00:50:16,764 --> 00:50:17,848
...friend...

644
00:50:18,849 --> 00:50:23,395
...when did Saruman the Wise
abandon reason for madness?

645
00:50:39,713 --> 00:50:46,888
{\an8}[CHORUS IN BLACK SPEECH]:
<i>One Ring for the Dark lord on his dark throne
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi)</font></i>

646
00:50:47,337 --> 00:51:00,267
{\an8}<i>In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

647
00:51:00,518 --> 00:51:20,918
{\an8}<i>One Ring for the Dark lord on his dark throne
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi)</font></i>

648
00:51:02,893 --> 00:51:04,603
I gave you the chance...

649
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:08,399
...of aiding me willingly...

650
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:12,736
...but you have elected
the way of pain!

651
00:51:36,010 --> 00:51:37,511
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

652
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:39,930
Frodo? Frodo!

653
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:44,602
-I thought I'd lost you.
-What are you talking about?

654
00:51:44,768 --> 00:51:47,771
-It's just something Gandalf said.
-What did he say?

655
00:51:48,606 --> 00:51:52,484
"Don't you lose him, Samwise Gamgee."
And I don't mean to.

656
00:51:52,735 --> 00:51:56,363
Sam, we're still in the Shire.
What could possibly happen?

657
00:51:59,325 --> 00:52:00,367
Frodo.

658
00:52:00,618 --> 00:52:02,870
-Merry, it's Frodo Baggins.
-Hello, Frodo.

659
00:52:03,037 --> 00:52:04,455
Get off him.

660
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:06,457
Come on, Frodo.

661
00:52:06,624 --> 00:52:08,500
FRODO:
What's the meaning of this?

662
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:10,711
You've been into Farmer Maggot's crop!

663
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:12,129
[DOG BARKS]

664
00:52:13,213 --> 00:52:15,341
MAGGOT:
You get back here!

665
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:17,676
Get out of my field!

666
00:52:17,843 --> 00:52:20,679
You'll know the devil
if I catch up with you!

667
00:52:20,888 --> 00:52:23,849
MERRY: I don't know why he's so upset.
It's only a couple of carrots.

668
00:52:24,016 --> 00:52:25,142
PIPPIN:
And some cabbages.

669
00:52:25,309 --> 00:52:28,228
And those three bags of potatoes
that we lifted last week.

670
00:52:28,395 --> 00:52:32,483
-And then the mushrooms the week before.
MERRY: Yes, Pippin. My point is...

671
00:52:32,691 --> 00:52:34,860
...he's clearly overreacting.

672
00:52:35,069 --> 00:52:36,570
Run!

673
00:52:50,042 --> 00:52:52,586
Oh, that was close.

674
00:52:53,671 --> 00:52:56,799
I think I've broken something.

675
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:00,177
Trust a Brandybuck and a Took!

676
00:53:00,344 --> 00:53:04,014
What? That was just a detour.
A short cut.

677
00:53:04,181 --> 00:53:06,433
-Short cut to what?
-Mushrooms!

678
00:53:15,192 --> 00:53:16,694
PIPPIN:
That's mine.

679
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,073
That's nice, Merry.

680
00:53:21,615 --> 00:53:23,617
MERRY:
Here's a nice one, Sam.

681
00:53:23,826 --> 00:53:26,370
I think we should get off the road.

682
00:53:27,955 --> 00:53:31,625
[SCREECHING]

683
00:53:35,546 --> 00:53:36,922
Get off the road!

684
00:53:37,131 --> 00:53:38,632
Quick!

685
00:53:46,974 --> 00:53:51,061
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

686
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:52,813
Be quiet!

687
00:54:19,923 --> 00:54:21,675
[SNIFFS]

688
00:54:43,338 --> 00:54:45,362
THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Lord...
<font color="#bd2600">(Durbgu...)</font></i>

689
00:54:59,129 --> 00:55:01,298
What was that?

690
00:55:17,038 --> 00:55:26,788
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> We take...
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêpâm nêd...)</font></i>

691
00:55:20,567 --> 00:55:22,694
[SCREECHES]

692
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:35,499
SAM:
Anything?

693
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,668
Nothing.

694
00:55:38,377 --> 00:55:40,671
What is going on?

695
00:55:41,213 --> 00:55:45,008
That Black Rider was looking
for something. Or someone.

696
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,845
Frodo?

697
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:49,596
Get down!

698
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:08,782
I have to leave the Shire.

699
00:56:09,783 --> 00:56:12,077
Sam and I must get to Bree.

700
00:56:12,286 --> 00:56:13,704
Right.

701
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:17,374
Bucklebury Ferry. Follow me.

702
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:27,009
PIPPIN:
Run!

703
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,220
MERRY:
This way! Follow me!

704
00:56:33,765 --> 00:56:34,808
PIPPIN:
Run!

705
00:56:38,771 --> 00:56:48,046
{\an8}<i>We renounce our Maker.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâbîtham Magânanê.)</font></i>

706
00:56:48,071 --> 00:56:49,823
MERRY:
Get the rope, Sam!

707
00:56:51,962 --> 00:56:56,318
{\an8}<i>The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd.)</font></i>

708
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:54,036
Frodo!

709
00:56:54,745 --> 00:56:56,163
PIPPIN:
Run, Frodo!

710
00:56:56,330 --> 00:57:06,072
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine from the darkness.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nidir nênâ dâur-ad.)</font></i>

711
00:56:56,496 --> 00:56:57,581
FRODO: Go!
PIPPIN: Hurry!

712
00:56:57,789 --> 00:57:00,417
MERRY:
Frodo, come on!

713
00:57:01,335 --> 00:57:03,337
SAM: Come on! Faster!
PIPPIN: Jump!

714
00:57:10,302 --> 00:57:11,803
[SCREECHES]

715
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:22,522
-How far to the nearest crossing?
-The Brandywine Bridge. 20 miles.

716
00:57:37,120 --> 00:57:38,622
Come on.

717
00:57:49,800 --> 00:57:53,220
-What do you want?
-We're heading for the Prancing Pony.

718
00:57:56,723 --> 00:57:59,559
Hobbits. Four Hobbits!

719
00:57:59,726 --> 00:58:03,689
What's more, out of the Shire by your
talk. What business brings you to Bree?

720
00:58:04,106 --> 00:58:07,234
We wish to stay at the inn.
Our business is our own.

721
00:58:08,235 --> 00:58:10,821
All right, young sir.
I meant no offense.

722
00:58:10,988 --> 00:58:13,532
It's my job to ask questions
after nightfall.

723
00:58:13,699 --> 00:58:16,535
There's talk of strange folk abroad.

724
00:58:16,702 --> 00:58:18,870
Can't be too careful.

725
00:58:38,598 --> 00:58:42,102
Out of the way!
Watch where you're walking.

726
00:58:49,443 --> 00:58:52,154
[LAUGHING]

727
00:59:06,251 --> 00:59:07,878
Excuse me.

728
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:11,715
Good evening, little masters.
What can I do for you?

729
00:59:11,882 --> 00:59:17,971
If you're seeking accommodation, we got
some cozy Hobbit-sized rooms available.

730
00:59:18,180 --> 00:59:22,809
Always proud to cater
to the Little Folk, Mister...?

731
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,021
Underhill. My name's Underhill.

732
00:59:27,314 --> 00:59:29,816
-Underhill, yes.
-We're friends of Gandalf the Grey.

733
00:59:29,983 --> 00:59:33,153
-Can you tell him we've arrived?
-Gandalf?

734
00:59:33,570 --> 00:59:35,322
Gandalf.

735
00:59:36,156 --> 00:59:37,824
Oh, yes...

736
00:59:38,033 --> 00:59:40,160
...I remember. Elderly chap.

737
00:59:40,494 --> 00:59:43,413
Big grey beard, pointy hat.

738
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:45,665
Not seen him for six months.

739
00:59:52,422 --> 00:59:53,715
What do we do now?

740
01:00:00,931 --> 01:00:02,182
Sam...

741
01:00:02,349 --> 01:00:04,226
...he'll be here. He'll come.

742
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:09,064
MAN:
Get out of my way!

743
01:00:11,441 --> 01:00:13,110
What's that?

744
01:00:13,360 --> 01:00:15,862
This, my friend, is a pint.

745
01:00:16,029 --> 01:00:17,697
It comes in pints?

746
01:00:18,031 --> 01:00:21,743
-I'm getting one.
-You got a whole half already!

747
01:00:28,083 --> 01:00:31,920
That fellow's done nothing
but stare at you since we arrived.

748
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:36,967
Excuse me.

749
01:00:38,760 --> 01:00:41,763
That Man in the corner. Who is he?

750
01:00:42,931 --> 01:00:47,352
He's one of them Rangers. They're
dangerous folk, wandering the Wilds.

751
01:00:47,602 --> 01:00:52,107
What his right name is, I've never heard,
but around here he's known as Strider.

752
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,735
Strider.

753
01:01:08,748 --> 01:01:11,960
VOICE OF THE RING:
<i>Baggins.</i>

754
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:16,965
<i>Baggins.</i>

755
01:01:22,345 --> 01:01:27,475
<i>Baggins. Baggins.</i>

756
01:01:29,311 --> 01:01:31,605
PIPPIN:
Baggins? Sure, I know a Baggins.

757
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:35,275
He's over there. Frodo Baggins.

758
01:01:35,442 --> 01:01:38,486
He's my second cousin,
once removed on his mother's side...

759
01:01:38,653 --> 01:01:40,947
...and my third cousin, twice removed...

760
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:47,204
-Pippin!
-Steady on, Frodo.

761
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:19,194
SAURON:
You cannot hide.

762
01:02:22,155 --> 01:02:24,603
I see you.

763
01:02:24,628 --> 01:02:26,969
[IN BLACK SPEECH] I smell your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font>

764
01:02:26,993 --> 01:02:29,704
There is no life...

765
01:02:29,871 --> 01:02:32,082
...in the void.

766
01:02:32,249 --> 01:02:33,388
Only...

767
01:02:33,413 --> 01:02:34,644
[IN BLACK SPEECH] ...your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(...sherkuk.)</font>

768
01:02:34,668 --> 01:02:36,169
...death.

769
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:47,055
You draw far too much attention
to yourself, "Mr. Underhill."

770
01:02:51,726 --> 01:02:52,769
What do you want?

771
01:02:52,978 --> 01:02:55,021
A little more caution from you.
That is no trinket you carry.

772
01:02:55,397 --> 01:02:58,400
-I carry nothing.
-Indeed.

773
01:02:58,692 --> 01:03:01,236
I can avoid being seen if I wish...

774
01:03:01,403 --> 01:03:05,115
...but to disappear entirely,
that is a rare gift.

775
01:03:05,615 --> 01:03:08,243
-Who are you?
-Are you frightened?

776
01:03:09,494 --> 01:03:10,537
Yes.

777
01:03:10,704 --> 01:03:14,624
Not nearly frightened enough.
I know what hunts you.

778
01:03:16,418 --> 01:03:17,877
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

779
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:21,172
Let him go!
Or I'll have you, Longshanks.

780
01:03:22,841 --> 01:03:26,970
You have a stout heart, little Hobbit.
But that will not save you.

781
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:30,056
You can no longer wait
for the wizard, Frodo.

782
01:03:30,223 --> 01:03:31,224
They're coming.

783
01:03:31,558 --> 01:03:34,394
[HORSE GRUNTS]

784
01:03:36,741 --> 01:03:40,605
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd)</font></i>

785
01:03:41,980 --> 01:03:47,180
{\an8}<i>Behold! The Nine!
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Nidir!)</font></i>

786
01:03:47,383 --> 01:03:51,399
{\an8}<i>We are... we take
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham... nêpâm)</font></i>

787
01:03:52,785 --> 01:03:57,505
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

788
01:04:41,378 --> 01:04:43,630
[SCREECHING]

789
01:04:54,933 --> 01:04:56,434
What are they?

790
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:00,730
They were once Men.

791
01:05:01,231 --> 01:05:03,441
Great kings of Men.

792
01:05:03,650 --> 01:05:06,820
Then Sauron the Deceiver gave to them
nine rings of power.

793
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:10,490
Blinded by their greed,
they took them without question.

794
01:05:10,740 --> 01:05:14,077
One by one, falling into darkness.

795
01:05:14,244 --> 01:05:16,746
Now they are slaves to his will.

796
01:05:19,124 --> 01:05:20,834
They are the Nazgûl.

797
01:05:21,000 --> 01:05:23,753
Ringwraiths. Neither living nor dead.

798
01:05:24,504 --> 01:05:25,964
At all times they feel...

799
01:05:26,131 --> 01:05:28,091
<i>...the presence of the Ring...</i>

800
01:05:28,258 --> 01:05:32,804
<i>...drawn to the power of the One.
They will never stop hunting you.</i>

801
01:05:42,772 --> 01:05:45,692
FRODO: Where are you taking us?
-Into the Wild.

802
01:05:53,867 --> 01:05:57,996
How do we know this Strider
is a friend of Gandalf?

803
01:05:58,163 --> 01:06:00,999
I think a servant of the enemy
would look fairer...

804
01:06:01,374 --> 01:06:05,295
-...and feel fouler.
-He's foul enough.

805
01:06:05,879 --> 01:06:08,715
We have no choice but to trust him.

806
01:06:08,882 --> 01:06:12,343
-But where is he leading us?
STRIDER: To Rivendell, Master Gamgee.

807
01:06:14,721 --> 01:06:18,016
-To the house of Elrond.
SAM: Did you hear that? Rivendell.

808
01:06:18,558 --> 01:06:21,352
We're going to see the Elves.

809
01:06:38,620 --> 01:06:40,246
[HOBBITS WHISPERING]

810
01:06:42,999 --> 01:06:47,253
-Gentlemen, we do not stop till nightfall.
-What about breakfast?

811
01:06:47,420 --> 01:06:50,089
-You've already had it.
-We've had one, yes.

812
01:06:50,256 --> 01:06:52,509
What about second breakfast?

813
01:06:55,929 --> 01:06:59,098
Don't think he knows
about second breakfast, Pip.

814
01:06:59,265 --> 01:07:04,521
What about elevenses? Luncheon?
Afternoon tea? Dinner? Supper?

815
01:07:04,729 --> 01:07:08,900
-He knows about them, doesn't he?
-I wouldn't count on it.

816
01:07:14,364 --> 01:07:15,949
MERRY:
Pippin!

817
01:07:32,465 --> 01:07:35,969
What do they eat
when they can't get Hobbit?

818
01:07:51,612 --> 01:07:54,297
STRIDER [SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Tinúviel the elven-fair,
<font color="#00bd00">(Tinúviel elvanui,)</font></i>

819
01:07:55,869 --> 01:07:59,325
<i>Immortal maiden...
<font color="#00bd00">(Elleth alfirin...)</font></i>

820
01:08:00,193 --> 01:08:02,112
<i>...elven-wise
<font color="#00bd00">(...edhelhael)</font></i>

821
01:08:03,788 --> 01:08:10,572
<i>About him cast her night-dark hair
<font color="#00bd00">(O hon ring finnil fuinui)</font></i>

822
01:08:11,673 --> 01:08:14,607
<i>And arms like silver...
<font color="#00bd00">(A renc gelebrin...)</font></i>

823
01:08:14,632 --> 01:08:16,843
Who is she?

824
01:08:17,510 --> 01:08:20,138
This woman you sing of.

825
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:25,977
'Tis the lady of Lúthien.

826
01:08:26,144 --> 01:08:31,316
The Elf-maiden who gave her love
to Beren, a mortal.

827
01:08:33,151 --> 01:08:35,278
What happened to her?

828
01:08:37,488 --> 01:08:39,991
She died.

829
01:08:44,037 --> 01:08:46,372
Get some sleep, Frodo.

830
01:08:56,633 --> 01:09:00,720
SARUMAN: <i> The power of Isengard
is at your command...</i>

831
01:09:00,887 --> 01:09:05,350
<i>...Sauron, Lord of the Earth.</i>

832
01:09:05,617 --> 01:09:08,353
[VOICES WHISPERING IN BLACK SPEECH]

833
01:09:08,686 --> 01:09:14,484
SAURON:
<i>Build me an army worthy of Mordor.</i>

834
01:09:20,198 --> 01:09:24,661
What orders from Mordor, my lord?
What does the Eye command?

835
01:09:25,078 --> 01:09:27,038
We have work to do.

836
01:10:09,622 --> 01:10:14,252
The trees are strong, my lord.
Their roots go deep.

837
01:10:14,627 --> 01:10:16,462
Rip them all down.

838
01:10:43,906 --> 01:10:46,784
This was the great watchtower
of Amon Sûl.

839
01:10:48,494 --> 01:10:51,164
We shall rest here tonight.

840
01:11:02,884 --> 01:11:06,304
These are for you.
Keep them close.

841
01:11:06,512 --> 01:11:09,015
I'm going to have a look around.

842
01:11:11,392 --> 01:11:13,311
Stay here.

843
01:11:15,855 --> 01:11:18,024
MERRY:
My tomato's burst.

844
01:11:18,274 --> 01:11:20,151
PIPPIN:
Could I have some bacon?

845
01:11:20,359 --> 01:11:22,320
MERRY:
Want a tomato, Sam?

846
01:11:22,695 --> 01:11:26,365
-What are you doing?!
-Tomatoes, sausages, nice crispy bacon.

847
01:11:26,532 --> 01:11:29,285
SAM: We saved some for you, Mr. Frodo.
FRODO: Put it out, you fools!

848
01:11:29,494 --> 01:11:33,498
-Put it out!
PIPPIN: That's nice! Ash on my tomatoes!

849
01:11:34,040 --> 01:11:36,167
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

850
01:11:41,923 --> 01:11:43,674
Go!

851
01:12:07,876 --> 01:12:11,925
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd.)</font></i>

852
01:12:13,278 --> 01:12:17,116
{\an8}<i>Behold! We, the Nine.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Nidir, nê.)</font></i>

853
01:12:18,806 --> 01:12:24,204
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves the power.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêpâm nêd abârat.)</font></i>

854
01:12:25,610 --> 01:12:29,751
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Dir nênâkham.)</font></i>

855
01:12:31,089 --> 01:12:41,543
{\an8}<i>We renounce our Maker.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâbîtham Magânanê.)</font></i>

856
01:12:37,103 --> 01:12:38,563
Back, you devils!

857
01:12:41,996 --> 01:12:48,014
{\an8}<i>We cleave the darkness.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêtabdam dâur.)</font></i>

858
01:12:49,031 --> 01:12:50,913
VOICE OF THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> In the void...
<font color="#bd2600">(Gûm-ishi...)</font></i>

859
01:12:53,014 --> 01:12:54,286
<i>Only...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ashi...)</font></i>

860
01:13:13,835 --> 01:13:15,336
<i>Death...
<font color="#bd2600">(Gurum...)</font></i>

861
01:13:30,516 --> 01:13:33,528
VOICE OF THE RING: <i> Where the Shadows lie...
<font color="#bd2600">(Makha Gulshu darulu...)</font></i>

862
01:13:33,808 --> 01:13:39,378
<i>In the Land of Mordor where Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

863
01:13:39,635 --> 01:13:41,959
[VOICE OF THE RING HISSES]

864
01:14:02,063 --> 01:14:03,314
Frodo!

865
01:14:07,360 --> 01:14:09,195
-Frodo.
-Oh, Sam.

866
01:14:46,232 --> 01:14:47,233
Strider!

867
01:14:50,027 --> 01:14:55,533
-Help him, Strider.
-He's been stabbed by a Morgul blade.

868
01:14:57,034 --> 01:15:01,914
This is beyond my skill to heal.
He needs Elvish medicine.

869
01:15:06,502 --> 01:15:07,545
Hurry!

870
01:15:07,753 --> 01:15:11,716
We're six days from Rivendell!
He'll never make it!

871
01:15:11,924 --> 01:15:13,759
Hold on, Frodo.

872
01:15:15,344 --> 01:15:16,387
Gandalf!

873
01:15:33,279 --> 01:15:36,407
[METAL CLANKING]

874
01:15:46,125 --> 01:15:52,864
{\an8}[SINGING IN QUENYA]: <i> The earth...
<font color="#0078bd">(I ce...)</font></i>

875
01:15:52,889 --> 01:16:03,508
{\an8}<i>The earth groans...
<font color="#0078bd">(I cemen nurrua...)</font></i>

876
01:16:03,774 --> 01:16:11,257
{\an8}<i>and the wind...
<font color="#0078bd">(ar i súre...)</font></i>

877
01:16:11,281 --> 01:16:16,736
{\an8}<i>the wind...
<font color="#0078bd">(i súre...)</font></i>

878
01:16:13,917 --> 01:16:20,793
[WHISPERS INSTRUCTIONS TO THE MOTH]

879
01:16:17,148 --> 01:16:24,455
{\an8}<i>is crying!
<font color="#0078bd">(naina!)</font></i>

880
01:17:09,750 --> 01:17:11,043
[GROWLS]

881
01:17:54,295 --> 01:17:57,381
Look, Frodo. It's Mr. Bilbo's trolls.

882
01:17:59,550 --> 01:18:02,386
Mr. Frodo? He's going cold.

883
01:18:05,347 --> 01:18:07,099
Is he going to die?

884
01:18:07,308 --> 01:18:12,188
He's passing into the Shadow World.
He'll soon become a Wraith like them.

885
01:18:12,438 --> 01:18:14,023
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

886
01:18:17,359 --> 01:18:21,197
-They're close.
-Sam, do you know the Athelas plant?

887
01:18:21,363 --> 01:18:22,865
-Athelas?
-Kingsfoil.

888
01:18:23,032 --> 01:18:24,116
Kingsfoil, aye, it's a weed.

889
01:18:24,325 --> 01:18:27,453
It may help to slow the poisoning.
Hurry!

890
01:18:41,842 --> 01:18:45,971
WOMAN: What's this?
A Ranger caught off his guard?

891
01:18:50,403 --> 01:19:14,853
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Tinúviel the elven-fair,
<font color="#00bd00">(Tinúviel elvanui,)</font></i>

892
01:19:10,871 --> 01:19:11,914
Frodo.

893
01:19:13,874 --> 01:19:17,100
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Im Arwen - telin le thaed.)</font>

894
01:19:14,856 --> 01:19:28,720
{\an8}<i>Immortal maiden...,
<font color="#00bd00">(Elleth alfirin e...)</font></i>

895
01:19:19,434 --> 01:19:21,301
<font color="#00bd00">(Lasto beth nîn...)</font>

896
01:19:21,519 --> 01:19:23,685
<font color="#00bd00">(Tolo dan nan galad.)</font>

897
01:19:28,847 --> 01:19:30,683
Who is she?

898
01:19:31,350 --> 01:19:33,102
Frodo.

899
01:19:33,352 --> 01:19:36,855
-She's an Elf.
-He's fading.

900
01:19:39,108 --> 01:19:41,277
[IN WESTRON]
He's not going to last.

901
01:19:41,485 --> 01:19:44,154
We must get him to my father.

902
01:19:44,905 --> 01:19:47,783
-I've been looking for you for two days.
-Where are you taking him?

903
01:19:47,950 --> 01:19:54,039
There are five Wraiths behind you.
Where the other four are, I do not know.

904
01:19:55,132 --> 01:19:57,675
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Dartho guin Beriain - rych le ad tolthathon.)</font>

905
01:19:57,700 --> 01:19:59,508
<font color="#00bd00">(Hon mabathon - rochon ellint im.)</font>

906
01:20:00,313 --> 01:20:01,718
<font color="#00bd00">(Andelu i ven.)</font>

907
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:03,132
What are they saying?

908
01:20:03,350 --> 01:20:05,479
ARWEN: [Frodo is dying.] <font color="#00bd00">(Frodo fîr. Ae athradon i hîr...)</font>

909
01:20:05,519 --> 01:20:08,230
<font color="#00bd00">(...tûr gwaith nîn beriatha hon.)</font>

910
01:20:09,221 --> 01:20:10,889
[IN WESTRON]
I do not fear them.

911
01:20:14,685 --> 01:20:16,645
[IN SINDARIN] As you wish.
<font color="#00bd00">(Be iest lîn.)</font>

912
01:20:20,733 --> 01:20:22,151
[IN WESTRON]
Arwen...

913
01:20:22,318 --> 01:20:24,682
...ride hard. Don't look back.

914
01:20:24,706 --> 01:20:26,913
[IN SINDARIN] Ride fast, Asfaloth, ride fast!
<font color="#00bd00">(Noro lim, Asfaloth, noro lim!)</font>

915
01:20:30,576 --> 01:20:34,955
What are you doing?!
Those Wraiths are still out there!

916
01:21:36,795 --> 01:21:40,975
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd.)</font></i>

917
01:21:41,814 --> 01:21:42,981
[SCREECHES]

918
01:21:42,270 --> 01:21:47,725
{\an8}<i>Behold! We are... we take
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Kham... nêpâm)</font></i>

919
01:21:45,109 --> 01:21:47,653
Ride fast, Asfaloth!
<font color="#00bd00">(Noro lim, Asfaloth!)</font>

920
01:21:47,747 --> 01:21:51,433
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

921
01:21:52,663 --> 01:21:57,963
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

922
01:21:57,988 --> 01:22:01,498
{\an8}<i>The Lords of Unending Life
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâ Katharâd)</font></i>

923
01:22:02,846 --> 01:22:07,996
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nidir nênâ)</font></i>

924
01:22:08,021 --> 01:22:16,321
{\an8}<i>We renounce the darkness
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbîtham [dâ]ur)</font></i>

925
01:22:29,570 --> 01:22:32,281
Give up the halfling, She-Elf.

926
01:22:33,198 --> 01:22:35,784
[IN WESTRON]
If you want him, come and claim him.

927
01:22:47,838 --> 01:22:50,176
[IN SINDARIN] Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word;
<font color="#00bd00">(Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer;)</font>

928
01:22:50,568 --> 01:22:53,515
flow waters of Loudwater, against the Ringwraiths!
<font color="#00bd00">(rimmo nîn Bruinen, dan in Ulaer!)</font>

929
01:22:53,706 --> 01:22:56,325
Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word;
<font color="#00bd00">(Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer;)</font>

930
01:22:56,873 --> 01:22:59,922
flow waters of Loudwater, against the Ringwraiths!
<font color="#00bd00">(rimmo nîn Bruinen, dan in Ulaer!)</font>

931
01:23:27,139 --> 01:23:59,939
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN WESTRON]:
<i> What Grace is given me, let it pass to him.</i>

932
01:23:29,671 --> 01:23:32,174
[IN WESTRON]
No. No!

933
01:23:35,427 --> 01:23:37,721
Frodo, no.

934
01:23:37,930 --> 01:23:40,224
Frodo, don't give in.

935
01:23:40,432 --> 01:23:42,434
Not now.

936
01:23:53,362 --> 01:23:55,864
ARWEN:
<i>What grace is given me...</i>

937
01:23:56,532 --> 01:23:58,367
<i>...let it pass to him.</i>

938
01:23:58,617 --> 01:24:00,744
<i>Let him be spared.</i>

939
01:23:59,968 --> 01:24:13,650
{\an8}<i>Let him be spared. Mighty Valar, save him.</i>

940
01:24:01,374 --> 01:24:03,417
<i>Save him.</i>

941
01:24:05,596 --> 01:24:10,009
[IN SINDARIN] Hear my voice. Come back to the light.
<font color="#00bd00">(Lasto beth nîn. Tolo dan nan galad.)</font>

942
01:24:15,801 --> 01:24:20,973
-Where am I?
GANDALF: You are in the house of Elrond.

943
01:24:21,431 --> 01:24:27,938
And it is 10:00 in the morning
on October 24th, if you want to know.

944
01:24:29,898 --> 01:24:33,694
-Gandalf!
-Yes, I'm here.

945
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:38,407
And you're lucky to be here too.

946
01:24:39,074 --> 01:24:43,078
A few more hours and you
would have been beyond our aid.

947
01:24:43,287 --> 01:24:47,416
But you have some strength in you,
my dear Hobbit.

948
01:24:55,007 --> 01:24:57,509
What happened, Gandalf?

949
01:24:58,468 --> 01:25:03,849
-Why didn't you meet us?
-I am sorry, Frodo.

950
01:25:08,604 --> 01:25:10,355
I was delayed.

951
01:25:11,231 --> 01:25:15,444
A friendship with Saruman
is not lightly thrown aside.

952
01:25:19,531 --> 01:25:24,202
One ill turn deserves another.
It is over.

953
01:25:24,494 --> 01:25:27,247
Embrace the power of the Ring...

954
01:25:25,433 --> 01:25:30,565
{\an8}[SINGING IN QUENYA] <i> The earth...
<font color="#0078bd">(I ce...)</font></i>

955
01:25:27,789 --> 01:25:30,334
...or embrace your own destruction!

956
01:25:32,628 --> 01:25:36,506
GANDALF:
There is only one Lord of the Ring.

957
01:25:36,757 --> 01:25:42,860
{\an8}<i>The earth...
<font color="#0078bd">(I ce...)</font></i>

958
01:25:36,757 --> 01:25:40,761
Only one who can bend it to his will.

959
01:25:41,553 --> 01:25:45,515
And he does not share power.

960
01:25:45,766 --> 01:25:48,518
[BIRD SCREECHES]

961
01:25:59,863 --> 01:26:03,241
So you have chosen death.

962
01:26:13,293 --> 01:26:17,089
Gandalf? What is it?

963
01:26:18,048 --> 01:26:19,841
Nothing, Frodo.

964
01:26:20,509 --> 01:26:22,344
SAM:
Frodo!

965
01:26:22,552 --> 01:26:23,595
Frodo!

966
01:26:23,804 --> 01:26:26,181
-Sam.
-Bless you, you're awake!

967
01:26:26,390 --> 01:26:29,101
Sam has hardly left your side.

968
01:26:29,351 --> 01:26:31,520
We were that worried about you.
Weren't we, Mr. Gandalf?

969
01:26:31,895 --> 01:26:37,025
By the skills of Lord Elrond,
you're beginning to mend.

970
01:26:38,527 --> 01:26:42,114
Welcome to Rivendell, Frodo Baggins.

971
01:26:44,363 --> 01:27:04,182
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Here Elbereth Star-kindler,
<font color="#00bd00">(Nef Elbereth Gilthoniel,)</font></i>

972
01:27:04,446 --> 01:27:26,066
{\an8}<i>Glittering slants down like sparkling jewels
<font color="#00bd00">(Silivren penna míriel)</font></i>

973
01:27:30,162 --> 01:27:33,498
FRODO: Bilbo!
-Hello, Frodo, my lad.

974
01:27:33,665 --> 01:27:35,375
Bilbo.

975
01:27:40,380 --> 01:27:42,132
FRODO:
<i>"There and Back Again:</i>

976
01:27:42,382 --> 01:27:45,135
<i>A Hobbit's Tale</i>, by Bilbo Baggins."

977
01:27:48,180 --> 01:27:51,767
-This is wonderful.
-I meant to go back...

978
01:27:52,100 --> 01:27:55,896
...wonder at the powers of Mirkwood...

979
01:27:56,354 --> 01:27:58,648
...visit Lake-town...

980
01:27:58,899 --> 01:28:02,277
...see the Lonely Mountain again.

981
01:28:02,694 --> 01:28:07,616
But age, it seems,
has finally caught up with me.

982
01:28:19,711 --> 01:28:21,505
FRODO:
I miss the Shire.

983
01:28:21,922 --> 01:28:27,052
I spent all my childhood pretending
I was off somewhere else.

984
01:28:27,385 --> 01:28:30,972
Off with you,
on one of your adventures.

985
01:28:33,934 --> 01:28:37,521
But my own adventure turned out
to be quite different.

986
01:28:42,734 --> 01:28:45,946
I'm not like you, Bilbo.

987
01:28:47,072 --> 01:28:49,407
My dear boy.

988
01:28:53,495 --> 01:28:57,457
SAM: Now, what have I forgotten?
-Packed already?

989
01:28:56,081 --> 01:29:03,126
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Elbereth Star...
<font color="#00bd00">(Elbereth Gil...)</font></i>

990
01:28:58,250 --> 01:29:00,043
No harm in being prepared.

991
01:29:00,252 --> 01:29:02,838
-I thought you wanted to see the Elves.
-I do.

992
01:29:03,004 --> 01:29:05,924
-More than anything.
-I did.

993
01:29:06,091 --> 01:29:08,009
It's just...

994
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:11,429
We did what Gandalf wanted, didn't we?

995
01:29:11,596 --> 01:29:15,267
We got the Ring this far,
to Rivendell. And I thought...

996
01:29:15,475 --> 01:29:18,770
...seeing as how you're on the mend,
we'd be off soon.

997
01:29:18,979 --> 01:29:20,689
Off home.

998
01:29:24,860 --> 01:29:26,862
You are right, Sam.

999
01:29:29,030 --> 01:29:31,783
We did what we set out to do.

1000
01:29:32,367 --> 01:29:34,953
The Ring will be safe in Rivendell.

1001
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:41,376
I am ready to go home.

1002
01:29:42,127 --> 01:29:44,212
ELROND:
His strength returns.

1003
01:29:44,379 --> 01:29:50,093
That wound will never fully heal.
He will carry it the rest of his life.

1004
01:29:50,635 --> 01:29:53,221
And yet to have come so far
still bearing the Ring...

1005
01:29:53,388 --> 01:29:57,100
...the Hobbit has shown extraordinary
resilience to its evil.

1006
01:29:57,309 --> 01:30:00,645
It is a burden he should never
have had to bear.

1007
01:30:00,896 --> 01:30:06,318
-We can ask no more of Frodo.
-Gandalf, the enemy is moving.

1008
01:30:06,526 --> 01:30:11,156
Sauron's forces are massing in the East.
His Eye is fixed on Rivendell.

1009
01:30:11,406 --> 01:30:14,159
And Saruman, you tell me, has betrayed us.

1010
01:30:14,326 --> 01:30:17,579
Our list of allies grows thin.

1011
01:30:18,330 --> 01:30:21,124
His treachery runs deeper
than you know.

1012
01:30:21,333 --> 01:30:25,003
By foul craft, Saruman
has crossed Orcs with Goblin-men.

1013
01:30:25,170 --> 01:30:27,631
He's breeding an army
in the caverns of Isengard.

1014
01:30:27,923 --> 01:30:32,510
An army that can move in sunlight
and cover great distance at speed.

1015
01:30:32,677 --> 01:30:35,096
Saruman is coming for the Ring.

1016
01:30:35,555 --> 01:30:39,601
This evil cannot be concealed
by the power of the Elves.

1017
01:30:39,809 --> 01:30:44,189
We do not have the strength
to fight both Mordor and Isengard!

1018
01:30:48,026 --> 01:30:49,110
Gandalf...

1019
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:53,031
...the Ring cannot stay here.

1020
01:31:12,550 --> 01:31:15,720
ELROND: <i> This peril belongs
to all Middle-earth.</i>

1021
01:31:15,971 --> 01:31:18,682
<i>They must decide now how to end it.</i>

1022
01:31:19,724 --> 01:31:23,311
The time of the Elves is over.
My people are leaving these shores.

1023
01:31:23,979 --> 01:31:27,565
Who will you look to when we've gone?
The Dwarves?

1024
01:31:27,732 --> 01:31:32,862
They hide in mountains seeking riches.
They care not for the troubles of others.

1025
01:31:34,489 --> 01:31:37,325
It is in Men
that we must place our hope.

1026
01:31:37,659 --> 01:31:39,369
Men?

1027
01:31:40,245 --> 01:31:43,498
Men are weak.
The race of Men is failing.

1028
01:31:43,665 --> 01:31:48,128
The blood of Númenor is all but spent,
its pride and dignity forgotten.

1029
01:31:48,420 --> 01:31:51,923
It is because of Men
the Ring survives.

1030
01:31:52,132 --> 01:31:53,758
I was there, Gandalf.

1031
01:31:54,426 --> 01:31:57,262
<i>I was there 3000 years ago...</i>

1032
01:32:04,102 --> 01:32:06,521
<i>...when Isildur took the Ring.</i>

1033
01:32:06,688 --> 01:32:10,608
I was there the day
the strength of Men failed.

1034
01:32:13,153 --> 01:32:15,697
Isildur, hurry! Follow me.

1035
01:32:17,282 --> 01:32:20,910
ELROND: <i> I led Isildur into the heart
of Mount Doom...</i>

1036
01:32:21,161 --> 01:32:24,706
<i>...where the Ring was forged,
the one place it could be destroyed.</i>

1037
01:32:24,873 --> 01:32:27,459
Cast it into the fire!

1038
01:32:27,792 --> 01:32:30,628
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1039
01:32:32,630 --> 01:32:36,426
-Destroy it!
-No.

1040
01:32:37,761 --> 01:32:39,929
Isildur!

1041
01:32:40,388 --> 01:32:45,143
ELROND: <i> It should have ended that day,
but evil was allowed to endure.</i>

1042
01:32:49,230 --> 01:32:53,485
Isildur kept the Ring.
The line of kings is broken.

1043
01:32:54,402 --> 01:32:58,073
There's no strength left
in the world of Men.

1044
01:32:58,239 --> 01:33:03,078
-They're scattered, divided, leaderless.
-There is one who could unite them.

1045
01:33:03,286 --> 01:33:06,664
One who could reclaim
the throne of Gondor.

1046
01:33:08,333 --> 01:33:12,170
He turned from that path
a long time ago.

1047
01:33:12,337 --> 01:33:14,464
He has chosen exile.

1048
01:33:45,703 --> 01:33:47,705
You are no Elf.

1049
01:33:47,872 --> 01:33:49,958
Men of the South are welcome here.

1050
01:33:50,542 --> 01:33:54,045
-Who are you?
-I am a friend to Gandalf the Grey.

1051
01:33:55,547 --> 01:33:58,383
Then we are here on common purpose...

1052
01:33:58,758 --> 01:34:00,218
...friend.

1053
01:34:15,400 --> 01:34:18,319
The shards of Narsil.

1054
01:34:21,781 --> 01:34:26,244
The blade that cut the Ring
from Sauron's hand.

1055
01:34:29,164 --> 01:34:31,416
It's still sharp.

1056
01:34:40,300 --> 01:34:43,386
But no more than a broken heirloom.

1057
01:35:10,205 --> 01:35:13,249
Why do you fear the past?

1058
01:35:14,125 --> 01:35:19,464
You are Isildur's heir,
not Isildur himself.

1059
01:35:19,714 --> 01:35:23,134
You are not bound to his fate.

1060
01:35:23,635 --> 01:35:27,639
The same blood flows in my veins.

1061
01:35:30,642 --> 01:35:33,228
The same weakness.

1062
01:35:35,939 --> 01:35:38,733
Your time will come.

1063
01:35:38,942 --> 01:35:43,321
You will face the same evil.
And you will defeat it.

1064
01:35:46,459 --> 01:35:48,921
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(A si i-Dhúath ú-orthor, Aragorn.)</font>

1065
01:35:49,904 --> 01:35:53,506
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú or le... a ú or nin.)</font>

1066
01:36:00,015 --> 01:36:12,315
{\an8}[SINGING IN SINDARIN]: <i> From darkness I understand the night:
<font color="#00bd00">(O mór henion I dhû:)</font></i>

1067
01:36:04,850 --> 01:36:08,097
<font color="#00bd00">(Renich i lú i erui govannem?)</font>

1068
01:36:11,641 --> 01:36:16,187
<font color="#00bd00">(Nauthannen i ned ôl reniannen.)</font>

1069
01:36:13,911 --> 01:36:20,262
{\an8}<i>Dreams flow...
<font color="#00bd00">(Ely siriar...)</font></i>

1070
01:36:16,716 --> 01:36:19,243
<font color="#00bd00">(Gwenwin in enninath.)</font>

1071
01:36:20,275 --> 01:36:49,590
{\an8}<i>Ah! I desire Evenstar
<font color="#00bd00">(Ai! Aníron Undómiel)</font></i>

1072
01:36:20,915 --> 01:36:24,315
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú-'arnech in naeth i si celich.)</font>

1073
01:36:25,752 --> 01:36:27,829
<font color="#00bd00">(Renich i beth i pennen?)</font>

1074
01:36:33,871 --> 01:36:36,541
[IN WESTRON]
You said you'd bind yourself to me...

1075
01:36:38,543 --> 01:36:43,548
...forsaking the immortal life
of your people.

1076
01:36:44,674 --> 01:36:46,551
[IN WESTRON]
And to that I hold.

1077
01:36:46,694 --> 01:36:50,322
I would rather share
one lifetime with you...

1078
01:36:50,596 --> 01:36:54,475
...than face all the Ages
of this world alone.

1079
01:36:50,699 --> 01:37:02,499
{\an8}<i>Look! A star rises out of the darkness.
<font color="#00bd00">(Tiro! Êl eria e môr.)</font></i>

1080
01:37:03,234 --> 01:37:06,696
I choose a mortal life.

1081
01:37:03,720 --> 01:37:17,607
{\an8}<i>The song of the star enchants my heart.
<font color="#00bd00">(I ‘lîr en êl luitha ‘úren.)</font></i>

1082
01:37:18,096 --> 01:37:32,893
{\an8}<i>Ah! I desire...
<font color="#00bd00">(Ai! Aníron...)</font></i>

1083
01:37:08,031 --> 01:37:12,285
-You cannot give me this.
-It is mine to give to whom I will...

1084
01:37:15,538 --> 01:37:18,041
...like my heart.

1085
01:37:33,806 --> 01:37:37,518
ELROND: Strangers from distant lands,
friends of old...

1086
01:37:37,727 --> 01:37:41,647
...you've been summoned here
to answer the threat of Mordor.

1087
01:37:42,273 --> 01:37:47,153
Middle-earth stands upon the brink
of destruction. None can escape it.

1088
01:37:47,403 --> 01:37:50,907
You will unite, or you will fall.

1089
01:37:51,115 --> 01:37:55,411
Each race is bound to this fate,
this one doom.

1090
01:37:57,246 --> 01:38:00,750
Bring forth the Ring, Frodo.

1091
01:38:14,806 --> 01:38:16,557
So it is true.

1092
01:38:33,991 --> 01:38:36,119
In a dream...

1093
01:38:37,703 --> 01:38:40,832
...I saw the eastern sky grow dark...

1094
01:38:41,124 --> 01:38:42,834
...but in the West
a pale light lingered.

1095
01:38:43,626 --> 01:38:45,378
A voice was crying:

1096
01:38:45,670 --> 01:38:48,589
"Your doom is near at hand.

1097
01:38:49,590 --> 01:38:52,343
Isildur's Bane is found."

1098
01:38:54,563 --> 01:38:56,322
THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> In the cold...
<font color="#bd2600">(Kelkum-ishi...)</font></i>

1099
01:38:56,347 --> 01:38:58,182
Isildur's Bane.

1100
01:38:58,850 --> 01:38:59,482
Boromir!

1101
01:38:59,507 --> 01:39:01,940
[CHANTS IN BLACK SPEECH] One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font>

1102
01:39:00,665 --> 01:39:02,809
{\an8}[THE RING]: <i> Three Rings for the Elven-kings...
<font color="#bd2600">(Shre nazg golugranu...)</font></i>

1103
01:39:03,186 --> 01:39:06,695
...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font>

1104
01:39:03,188 --> 01:39:06,495
{\an8}<i>I smell your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font></i>

1105
01:39:06,596 --> 01:39:08,295
{\an8}<i>Seven for the Dwarf-lords.
<font color="#bd2600">(Ombi kuzddurbagu.)</font></i>

1106
01:39:07,060 --> 01:39:09,823
...One Ring to bring them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg thrakatulûk...)</font>

1107
01:39:09,508 --> 01:39:11,289
{\an8}<i>I smell your blood.</i>
<i><font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font></i>

1108
01:39:11,314 --> 01:39:13,014
{\an8}<i>In the cold... One for the Dark Lord...
<font color="#bd2600">(Kelkum-ishi... Ash Burz-Durbagu...)</font></i>

1109
01:39:13,039 --> 01:39:15,284
...and in the darkness...
<font color="#bd2600">(...agh burzum-ishi...)</font>

1110
01:39:13,031 --> 01:39:15,274
{\an8}<i>...in the darkness...
<font color="#bd2600">(...burzum-ishi...)</font></i>

1111
01:39:15,309 --> 01:39:17,027
...bind them!
<font color="#bd2600">(...krimpatul!)</font>

1112
01:39:23,332 --> 01:39:27,170
Never before has any voice uttered the
words of that tongue here in Imladris.

1113
01:39:27,336 --> 01:39:31,048
[IN WESTRON] I do not ask your pardon,
Master Elrond...

1114
01:39:31,215 --> 01:39:33,342
...for the Black Speech of Mordor...

1115
01:39:33,634 --> 01:39:35,011
...may yet be heard...

1116
01:39:35,178 --> 01:39:38,181
...in every corner of the West!

1117
01:39:38,347 --> 01:39:41,017
The Ring is altogether evil.

1118
01:39:41,350 --> 01:39:42,852
It is a gift.

1119
01:39:43,436 --> 01:39:45,521
A gift to the foes of Mordor.

1120
01:39:46,147 --> 01:39:48,232
Why not use this Ring?

1121
01:39:48,441 --> 01:39:51,194
Long has my father,
the Steward of Gondor...

1122
01:39:51,402 --> 01:39:55,740
...kept the forces of Mordor at bay.
By the blood of our people...

1123
01:39:56,032 --> 01:39:58,242
...are your lands kept safe.

1124
01:40:00,036 --> 01:40:04,373
Give Gondor the weapon of the enemy.
Let us use it against him.

1125
01:40:04,665 --> 01:40:08,419
You cannot wield it.
None of us can.

1126
01:40:09,045 --> 01:40:13,090
The One Ring answers to Sauron alone.
It has no other master.

1127
01:40:13,257 --> 01:40:16,802
And what would a Ranger know
of this matter?

1128
01:40:17,094 --> 01:40:19,096
This is no mere Ranger.

1129
01:40:20,097 --> 01:40:23,768
He is Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

1130
01:40:24,268 --> 01:40:27,188
You owe him your allegiance.

1131
01:40:31,275 --> 01:40:33,194
Aragorn.

1132
01:40:34,946 --> 01:40:37,782
This is Isildur's heir?

1133
01:40:40,117 --> 01:40:42,828
And heir to the throne of Gondor.

1134
01:40:44,924 --> 01:40:46,422
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Havo dad, Legolas.)</font>

1135
01:40:49,794 --> 01:40:52,630
Gondor has no king.

1136
01:40:54,465 --> 01:40:56,133
Gondor needs no king.

1137
01:41:02,807 --> 01:41:06,477
Aragorn is right. We cannot use it.

1138
01:41:07,478 --> 01:41:10,982
You have only one choice.

1139
01:41:11,232 --> 01:41:13,609
The Ring must be destroyed.

1140
01:41:15,444 --> 01:41:18,531
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1141
01:41:18,823 --> 01:41:21,367
What are we waiting for?

1142
01:41:26,835 --> 01:41:29,955
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where...
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha...)</font></i>

1143
01:41:30,308 --> 01:41:31,625
{\an8}<i>...your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(...sherkuk.)</font></i>

1144
01:41:33,504 --> 01:41:36,507
The Ring cannot be destroyed, Gimli,
son of Glóin...

1145
01:41:36,757 --> 01:41:41,012
...by any craft that we here possess.

1146
01:41:41,505 --> 01:41:44,482
The Ring was made in the fires
of Mount Doom.

1147
01:41:44,506 --> 01:41:49,687
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

1148
01:41:45,850 --> 01:41:49,687
Only there can it be unmade.

1149
01:41:50,730 --> 01:41:53,357
It must be taken deep into Mordor...

1150
01:41:53,529 --> 01:41:56,862
...and cast back into the fiery chasm
from whence it came.

1151
01:41:56,887 --> 01:42:00,506
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie...
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu...)</font></i>

1152
01:42:00,531 --> 01:42:02,533
One of you...

1153
01:42:03,034 --> 01:42:05,202
...must do this.

1154
01:42:08,122 --> 01:42:11,834
One does not simply walk into Mordor.

1155
01:42:12,710 --> 01:42:16,380
Its Black Gates are guarded
by more than just Orcs.

1156
01:42:17,214 --> 01:42:21,344
There is evil there
that does not sleep.

1157
01:42:21,552 --> 01:42:25,765
The Great Eye is ever-watchful.

1158
01:42:26,557 --> 01:42:28,559
It is a barren wasteland...

1159
01:42:28,768 --> 01:42:32,396
...riddled with fire, and ash
and dust.

1160
01:42:32,563 --> 01:42:36,400
The very air you breathe
is a poisonous fume.

1161
01:42:36,651 --> 01:42:40,905
Not with 10,000 men
could you do this. It is folly.

1162
01:42:41,155 --> 01:42:45,576
Have you heard nothing Lord Elrond
has said? The Ring must be destroyed.

1163
01:42:45,785 --> 01:42:48,412
And I suppose you think
you are the one to do it!

1164
01:42:48,579 --> 01:42:53,250
And if we fail, what then? What happens
when Sauron takes back what is his?

1165
01:42:53,417 --> 01:42:58,756
I will be dead before I see the Ring
in the hands of an Elf!

1166
01:42:58,923 --> 01:43:00,549
[SHOUTING]

1167
01:43:00,758 --> 01:43:03,260
Never trust an Elf!

1168
01:43:04,361 --> 01:43:08,036
GANDALF:
Do you not understand? While you bicker amongst yourselves,

1169
01:43:08,061 --> 01:43:10,267
Sauron's power grows!

1170
01:43:08,063 --> 01:43:10,267
{\an8}THE RING: <i>One Ring to rule them all... <font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1171
01:43:10,601 --> 01:43:13,553
None can escape it! You'll all be destroyed!

1172
01:43:10,599 --> 01:43:13,549
{\an8}<i>One Ring to find them... <font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1173
01:43:14,481 --> 01:43:16,787
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1174
01:43:16,812 --> 01:43:18,821
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1175
01:43:18,845 --> 01:43:21,347
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1176
01:43:21,371 --> 01:43:23,534
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1177
01:43:23,559 --> 01:43:25,729
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1178
01:43:25,753 --> 01:43:27,869
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1179
01:43:27,893 --> 01:43:29,582
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1180
01:43:32,248 --> 01:43:34,458
I will take it.

1181
01:43:36,460 --> 01:43:38,963
I will take it.

1182
01:43:44,802 --> 01:43:47,847
I will take the Ring to Mordor.

1183
01:43:55,896 --> 01:43:57,148
Though...

1184
01:44:00,234 --> 01:44:02,069
...I do not know the way.

1185
01:44:04,071 --> 01:44:08,409
I will help you bear
this burden, Frodo Baggins...

1186
01:44:08,576 --> 01:44:11,954
...as long as it is yours to bear.

1187
01:44:13,080 --> 01:44:16,167
If by my life
or death I can protect you...

1188
01:44:16,917 --> 01:44:18,252
...I will.

1189
01:44:21,464 --> 01:44:23,758
You have my sword.

1190
01:44:25,593 --> 01:44:27,678
And you have my bow.

1191
01:44:28,262 --> 01:44:30,765
And my ax.

1192
01:44:37,772 --> 01:44:40,775
You carry the fates
of us all, little one.

1193
01:44:42,777 --> 01:44:46,447
If this is indeed
the will of the Council...

1194
01:44:46,906 --> 01:44:49,325
-...then Gondor will see it done.
-Hey!

1195
01:44:51,952 --> 01:44:56,707
-Frodo's not going anywhere without me.
-It is hardly possible to separate you...

1196
01:44:56,916 --> 01:45:01,796
...even when he is summoned
to a secret Council and you are not.

1197
01:45:02,296 --> 01:45:04,256
We're coming too!

1198
01:45:06,383 --> 01:45:09,136
You'll have to send us home
tied up in a sack to stop us.

1199
01:45:09,386 --> 01:45:12,723
Anyway, you need people
of intelligence on this sort of...

1200
01:45:13,057 --> 01:45:14,391
...mission.

1201
01:45:14,558 --> 01:45:16,060
Quest.

1202
01:45:16,519 --> 01:45:17,561
Thing.

1203
01:45:19,396 --> 01:45:22,066
Well, that rules you out, Pip.

1204
01:45:23,651 --> 01:45:25,569
Nine companions.

1205
01:45:27,404 --> 01:45:29,240
So be it.

1206
01:45:29,573 --> 01:45:32,576
You shall be
the Fellowship of the Ring.

1207
01:45:33,244 --> 01:45:35,079
Great!

1208
01:45:35,287 --> 01:45:37,581
Where are we going?

